        "date": "2026-11-22T15:16:42Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(turning): part off toward the chuck, never by the stock overhang\n\nSecond read of PR #3472: a plane inside the model took its scrap side\nfrom how far the stock ran past each model end. A model with its grip\nstub (Z-84..0, plane Z-70) under a stock with a 0.1 mm front facing\nallowance parted Z-70..-67, 3 mm into the part, and the verdict used the\nsame rule and stayed silent.\n\n- motion: the scrap side is the chuck side (parting_law::chuck_side).\n  No setup or machine states which spindle holds the bar, so it is ISO\n  841's -Z; each part-off path carries CHUCK_NOTE that says so. A plane\n  with the whole model on the chuck side is refused by name.\n- motion/app: part_kerf_refusal reads the side from the chuck alone,\n  not from the kernel's kerf, and refuses a band that takes model\n  material on the part side.\n- tests: turning_part_kerf gains the stubbed-model case with front\n  allowances 0, 0.1, 1 and 5 mm, the refusal of a model wholly on the\n  chuck side, and a hand-built kerf on the part side; turning_blade's\n  z 50 refusal text follows. Catalog .camproj files carry the note.\n\nFixes #3452\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
