        "date": "2026-11-22T15:46:53Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(turning): read the free end on the part's own axis; stale old part-offs\n\nThird read of PR #3472:\n\nA. The door tested document +Z. A model drawn lying down (along X) is\n   stood up with TURN, so document Z maps to horizontal in OP10 and in an\n   OP20 flip alike, and the flip passed. The kept side matters only when\n   the model goes on past the plane on both sides; there the Part arm now\n   refuses with setup_align::part_off_problem, which fits the part's own\n   turning axis (multiaxis::axis::fit) on the setup-frame facets and reads\n   it back into the document frame. A part modelled standing must point\n   its document-up end up the spindle by 0.5 or more (end for end at\n   -0.5 or less, no clear hold between; never a decision at 0). A part\n   modelled lying down has no as-modelled hold, so the setup cannot say\n   which end is free: refused. At an end of the model the model is the\n   part and any setup generates.\n\nB. A project saved before this change kept its cached part-off Ok, and\n   posted the old centred kerf. The Part stamp carries the salt\n   part-off-kerf-side-v1, so such a path loads Stale and the post refuses\n   it until it is generated again. The other blade kinds keep their\n   stamps.\n\nTests: lathe_part_off_kerf (lying pin under TURN generates at its end,\nlying stub refused under TURN and TURN turned end for end, a spin about\nthe spindle keeps the hold, the flip refused, the flipped part-only pin\nrefused by no_part_past_plane); part_off_saved_before_3452 with a\nfixture recorded on main 6679b1b4b; setup_align_lathe drops its PT1 (a\nlying bar with the plane inside the model, now refused by name).\n\nFixes #3452\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
